The Eulerian number \(a(n, m)\), denoted as \(a(n, m)\), counts the number of permutations of the sequence \([1, 2, \ldots, n]\) that have \(m\) ascents. An ascent occurs if a number is followed by a larger number in the sequence. The formula for the Eulerian number can be derived using the following recurrence relation:

\[ a(n, m) = (m + 1) \cdot a(n-1, m) - a(n-1, m) \]
